# Adversarial worst-case path corpus for the published benchmark matrix.
#
# This is the w = 3 instance (the base cell's 1,000 routes) of a generated
# family: corpus::path_expr(PathCorpus::AdversarialWorstCase, routes) derives
# the regex for any other power-of-ten route count by substituting the digit
# count in the {3} group below. Paired with the SharedPrefix route shape
# (corpus::route_table), the GitHub-like shape (most routes sharing the
# dynamic prefix /repos/acme/rNNN/issues/) chosen to force the deepest trie
# descent and the largest number of predicate evaluations over a maximal
# shared prefix. Every expansion of this regex names exactly one route in
# that table.
#
# Any tool that expands this pattern with an unbounded repetition operator
# (this one has none) must pass --max-repeat 4, so a future edit that adds
# one is still bounded. See MAX_REGEX_REPEAT in crates/irontraffic-bench/src/corpus.rs.
/repos/acme/r[0-9]{3}/issues/[0-9]{1,6}/(comments|reviews|files)
